+# VCF 9.1 architecture research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14.
+
+- **Product Interoperability Matrix — Broadcom**
+  https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability?col=1
+  Consulted the live selector for VMware product interoperability and upgrade
+  paths. The pinned snapshot remains the deterministic authority for the exact
+  source and target strings in `architecture.json`.
+
+- **Using the VMware Product Interoperability Matrixes — Broadcom Knowledge Base**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/343230
+  Confirmed that interoperability and upgrade paths are separate matrix views
+  and that patch releases must be shown when evaluating exact source versions.
+
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1 — Broadcom Knowledge Base**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630
+  Confirmed the VCF 9.0.x-to-9.1 path starts by upgrading VCF Operations and
+  then uses lifecycle workflows, and that the 9.0 Fleet Management Appliance
+  is replaced by VCF Management Services in 9.1.
+
+- **VCF 9.1 upgrade binaries do not show up in VCF Operations 9.0 — Broadcom Knowledge Base**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440282
+  Confirmed VCF Operations 9.1 precedes SDDC Manager and the remaining core
+  components.
+
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products — Broadcom Knowledge Base**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html
+  Confirmed the core order SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, vSAN witness, then ESXi
+  data hosts used by the pinned plan.
+
+- **Certificate Requirements for VCF Operations for Networks in VCF 9.1 — Broadcom Knowledge Base**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/424807
+  Confirmed the pre-upgrade gate that platform and collector certificates have
+  both FQDN and IP address SAN entries.
+
+No consulted source contradicted the compatibility combinations, order, or
+gates pinned in `fixtures/compatibility-snapshot.json`.
